1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:10,040
After each session, players are asked one thing: how hard was it?

2
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:17,495
They tap a value from 1 (very easy) to 10 (maximal). Nathan found Saturday’s match hard: 8.

3
00:00:17,495 --> 00:00:22,961
An optional comment, then Save. That’s it.

4
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:30,045
On the staff side, open Wellbeing › RPE. Every answer lands here, session by session.

5
00:00:30,045 --> 00:00:38,670
Player RPE, your own coach RPE, the gap between the two and the response rate over the last 4 weeks.

6
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:47,697
One row per player, one column per session. A big gap tells you a player feels sessions harder than you planned.

7
00:00:47,697 --> 00:00:57,476
Under Tracking › Load, RPE × minutes becomes each player’s load in arbitrary units (AU) — or GPS load once you import it.

8
00:00:57,476 --> 00:01:05,724
Players are sorted by load, highest first, with each one’s sessions, average RPE and share of the top load.

9
00:01:05,724 --> 00:01:15,105
The Trends tab ranks players by ACWR — this week’s load against the last four. The usual band is 0.8 to 1.3.

10
00:01:15,105 --> 00:01:21,778
When a player’s load jumps well above their own baseline, strivn raises a load alert.

11
00:01:21,778 --> 00:01:27,702
View trend shows the weekly load, ACWR, monotony and strain behind the alert.

12
00:01:27,702 --> 00:01:34,399
Adjust the plan, then acknowledge the alert so the whole staff knows it was handled.
